 \end{equation*}
 Under the assumption that the convex integrand $f$ satisfies a (partial) growth condition with respect to its gradient argument and a (partial) continuity condition with respect to its spatial argument, we demonstrate that, if the obstacle $\psi$ and the domain $\Omega$ possess $p+2$-bounded partial gradients, then the minimal solution $v$ exhibits corresponding regularity properties in the set $\partial_\Omega I_v$, where $v$ is the solution from the minimization problem and $\partial_\Omega$ denotes the portion of the boundary of the domain $\Omega$. Furthermore, we establish a partial version of the classical regularity theory for obstacles, demonstrating that, under sub-linear growth conditions, the solution $v$ exhibits expected regularity properties, provided the obstacle $\psi$ has corresponding regularity properties.
